# Environment variables

Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored — never commit it). Production values go in
Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.

```bash
# ── Masumi hosted preprod ──────────────────────────────────────
MASUMI_PAYMENT_API_URL=https://<provided-by-organizers>
MASUMI_API_KEY=<read-and-pay key>
MASUMI_REGISTRY_URL=https://<provided-by-organizers>

# ── Models (OpenAI primary, Groq/Gemini fallback via env swap) ──
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── Demo flags ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# false = real Masumi preprod escrows; true = labelled simulated ledger
SIMULATE_PAYMENTS=false
# live = full run; canned = replay of a recorded successful run
DEMO_MODE=live

# ── Outcome feed (demo-only signing key for simulated shop) ─────
# Generate locally: openssl rand -hex 32. Signs simulated conversions.
SHOP_SIGNING_KEY=
```

Rules: keys in Vercel env vars + `.env.local` only — never in the repo,
never in the browser, never on screen. Testnet tx hashes are public and
safe to commit.
